pub func:PRELUDE_SOURCE = string() never fails { pass "// The prelude — what the compiler itself declares.\n//\n// NOT COMPILED AS PART OF THE FRONTEND. Nothing `use`s this file. It is read by\n// `bootstrap/generator/gen_tables.py`, which emits it into\n// `src/frontend/prelude_source.npk` as a string constant, and the compiler then\n// puts that text through the same lexer, the same parser and the same collector as\n// any other module.\n//\n// SOURCE RATHER THAN SYNTHESIS, and generated rather than hand-escaped, for the two\n// reasons the token tables give: a declaration built in code is one a person cannot\n// read, and a constant written twice is one that can differ in one of the places.\n//\n// COLLECTED INTO THE ROOT SCOPE, so these names are in scope everywhere with no\n// import. Every module's scope has scope 0 as its parent, so the place already\n// existed.\n\nmod:prelude;\n\n// HOW TWO VALUES COMPARE, AS A TYPE RATHER THAN A NUMBER. The prototype's\n// `partial_cmp` returned an `int32` meaning less, equal or greater by sign — three\n// meanings in one number, which is the shape D-036 rejects for `bool` and `char`.\n// An ordering is not an integer either.\npub enum:Ordering = {\n    Less;\n    Equal;\n    Greater;\n};\n\n// EQUALITY. Derived field by field, in declaration order.\npub trait:Eq = {\n    func:eq = bool(Self:self, Self:other);\n};\n\n// A TOTAL ORDER. Every two values compare, which is what makes the result an\n// `Ordering` and not an `Ordering?`.\n//\n// The prototype generated `less_than` returning `bool`, which carries strictly less\n// information than a three-way comparison and made `Ord` WEAKER than `PartialOrd` —\n// backwards, since `Ord` is the stronger promise.\npub trait:Ord = {\n    func:cmp = Ordering(Self:self, Self:other);\n};\n\n// AN ORDER THAT MAY HAVE NO ANSWER. Not a second spelling of `Ord` but a different\n// promise, which is why it survives where `Display` did not: a `flt64` is IEEE 754\n// with `nan` and no trap (